  "root_causes": [
    "Nesso connected SX1262 only to GPIO SPI, leaving hardware SPI2 disconnected.",
    "SPI2 FIFO reads returned panel ID 0x81 instead of radio receive bytes.",
    "SPI2 UPDATE bit 23 was interpreted as SPI1 Flash block erase, injecting opcode D8 before each one-byte RadioLib transaction.",
    "The radio register model aliased 16-byte addresses and lacked continuous read/write and silicon identity."
  ],
  "independent_oracles": [
    "RadioLib 7.6.0 SX1262.h documents silicon identity SX1261 at the version register.",
    "ESP-IDF public SPI master and GPIO APIs send/read independently specified adjacent bytes 37 49."
  ],
